      "title": "Compare renewable and non-renewable resources",
      "explanation": "Renewable energy resources are replenished naturally on human timescales. They include sunlight, wind, moving water and sustainably managed biomass. Non-renewable resources, including fossil fuels and nuclear fuels, have finite supplies that are not replaced on the timescale of their use. Compare resources by availability, reliability, cost and environmental effects over their life cycle. Solar and wind output depend on weather, whereas some other renewables, such as geothermal energy, can provide steadier output. Biomass is only renewable in practice when material is replaced sufficiently quickly. No resource is impact-free. A country’s suitable mix depends on its location, demand, storage, grid connections and other constraints; there is no single best resource everywhere.",
