      "title": "Describe the live, neutral and earth wires in a plug",
      "explanation": "In a UK plug, three wires connect the appliance to the mains. The live wire carries the alternating mains supply; the neutral completes the circuit back to the supply; the earth provides a safety path for faults. The fuse sits in the live lead, so a fault will melt the fuse and break the circuit. Colour codes help: live is brown, neutral is blue, earth is green/yellow. A key safety point is that touching exposed metal is dangerous while plugged in; the earth path protects against shock by directing fault current away. Understanding these roles helps explain why fuses and proper wiring are essential for safety.",
