      "explanation": "The core skill is building a focused comparison from a shared idea. Begin with a concise statement about a theme or issue common to both poems. Structure the discussion so each verse or device from both poems is weighed against the same point, highlighting similarities and differences. Use language, form and structure as evidence, and note where the poets treat the idea differently or similarly. Keep the treatment balanced and avoid privileging one poem. Bring in context only to clarify interpretation if it genuinely deepens the point. Misconception: one poem is the model and the other merely supports; treat both as equal contributors to the idea.",
