      "title": "Use ruler and compass",
      "explanation": "Ruler and compass constructions produce exact shapes by copying lengths and angles with straight lines and circles, not by measuring. The compass transfers a distance by drawing circles with equal radii from known points; the intersections fix new points precisely. Arcs remain on the page as visible evidence of the method used. By using intersections of circles and straight lines you can construct perpendicular bisectors, angle bisectors, triangles and many other features with high accuracy. A common misconception is that you can simply measure a length with a ruler and place a point; accuracy comes from equal radii and precise intersection, not from measurement alone.",
