      "title": "Analyse global connections",
      "explanation": "Global connections are the flows of goods, capital, people and ideas across borders. They come via trade networks, transport routes, digital links and migration, creating interdependence and shifting where wealth is produced. Mechanisms include comparative advantage, outsourcing and multinational trade, plus exchange rates and policy choices. A common misconception is that openness always helps poorer economies; in reality, integration can bring volatility if domestic institutions are weak. A careful analysis highlights diversification, value‑added activity, fair trade and building domestic capacity to cope with shocks. Illustration: a simple chain of nodes across continents with arrows for goods, money and ideas.",
