      "title": "Explain the causes of uneven development",
      "explanation": "Uneven development arises from physical, historical and economic factors. Physical factors include climate, terrain and access to seas or rivers, which affect trade opportunities and resource availability. Historical factors involve the legacy of colonialism and inherited trade patterns that have favoured some places. Economic factors cover terms of trade, investment flows and global demand for certain goods, which can trap countries in low value‑adding activities. Political stability and governance also matter. A common misconception is that geography alone dictates outcomes; places with difficult geographies can prosper through policy and innovation. Illustration: a Venn diagram showing overlapping physical, historical and economic factors.",
