      "title": "Interpret unfamiliar maps",
      "explanation": "Interpreting unfamiliar maps means translating symbols, scales and colours into real geographical meaning. Start with the legend and scale to estimate distances, then check the north arrow and grid lines for orientation. Identify features from contours, land use symbols and water bodies, and use grid references to locate positions. Context is key: urban, coastal, rural or mountainous areas change interpretation. Misconception: a symbol on a map guarantees a ground feature exactly as shown; maps generalise and may omit details. Practice decoding one feature at a time and compare with what you know about the area.",
