      "title": "Present data using suitable graphs",
      "explanation": "Choosing the right graph is essential to communicate geographical patterns clearly. Use a scatter graph to explore relationships, a bar chart for comparisons, a line graph for change over time, and a histogram or box plot for distributions. Ensure axes are labelled with units, scales are even, and the graph has a clear title and, where needed, a legend. Avoid misleading scales or compressed axes that exaggerate differences. Refer to the graph in your write-up and quote key figures to back up any stated patterns or trends; a well-chosen graph should make the pattern obvious without extra explanation.",
