      "title": "Apply statistical skills to geographical data",
      "explanation": "Statistical work in geography combines measures of centre and spread with percentages to describe change and comparison. Compute the mean (sum ÷ count), the median or mode as appropriate, and the range (max − min) to convey spread. Use percentage change to express shifts over time or between places, with context. When data are split, consider the interquartile range (IQR) as a measure of spread for understanding variability. Always relate statistics to geographical meaning and note limitations, such as outliers or small samples, so conclusions remain grounded in the data rather than assumptions.",
