      "title": "Solve graphically",
      "explanation": "Solving graphically means finding the x-values where two graphs meet, so the equations share the same y-value. In practice you plot each rule on the same axes and identify the intersection points; those x-values solve the system. The method gives approximate solutions when the exact crossing is not obvious, or the functions are not easy to solve by algebra. Steps: plot each graph as accurately as possible, use the grid to read the x-coordinate at an intersection, then check by substituting back into one of the equations. A common misconception is that intersections must be at integer coordinates; in truth they can be decimals or fractions. If the crossing is faint, extend one graph or zoom to locate it more precisely.",
