      "title": "Use Venn diagrams for conditional events",
      "explanation": "Venn diagrams are a powerful visual tool for conditional events. Draw A and B, identify A∩B as the shared part, and use it to measure probabilities restricted to A. The conditional probability P(B|A) equals P(A∩B) divided by P(A); likewise P(A|B) = P(A∩B) / P(B). If A is a subset of B, P(B|A) equals 1; if A and B are disjoint, P(B|A) equals 0. These diagrams remind you that the denominator is the conditioning event and the numerator is the overlap. Use shading to keep track of the restricted space clearly.",
