      "title": "Distinguish radioactive contamination from irradiation",
      "explanation": "Distinguish radioactive contamination from irradiation: Irradiation means exposure to radiation from a source outside the material; the material does not become radioactive. Contamination means radioactive atoms are on or inside the material and can emit radiation themselves. External exposure depends on distance and shielding; internal exposure depends on ingestion or inhalation and how long the contaminant stays radioactive inside the body. Contaminated items require careful decontamination and safe handling to remove the radioactive atoms. Misconception: contamination is only a surface issue; internal contamination can be more dangerous because radiation is emitted inside the body.",
